1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:09,600
Many questions are yes or no: will this loan be repaid? Logistic regression gives a probability, not just a label.

2
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:16,900
The sigmoid squashes any score into a number between zero and one, like a dimmer switch.

3
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:24,325
A positive weight pushes towards yes. A negative weight pushes towards no.

4
00:00:25,030 --> 00:00:31,580
Missed payments might have a big negative weight on repayment. Income a positive one.

5
00:00:32,270 --> 00:00:38,370
That is why regulators like logistic regression: you can tell a customer why.

6
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:46,830
The business chooses the threshold. A careful bank might decline above thirty percent risk.

7
00:00:47,530 --> 00:00:57,655
Log loss punishes being confidently wrong. And each weight shows how a feature pushes the answer, which makes the model easy to explain.

